## refine(refinement, options)

### Description
Defines a custom validation refinement on a schema with an optional `when` callback to control whether the refinement runs based on prior validation status.

### Signature
```ts
schema.refine(refinementFn: (data: T) => boolean | Promise<boolean>, options?: {
  message?: string;
  path?: (string | number)[];
  when?: (payload: { value: unknown; issues: Array<{ path?: (string | number)[] }> }) => boolean;
})
```

### Options
- **message** (string, optional) - Custom error message to display when the refinement fails.
- **path** ((string | number)[], optional) - Key path indicating where the issue should be attached.
- **when** (function, optional) - Callback returning a boolean indicating if the refinement should execute given the current parse `payload`.

### Example (Zod)
```ts
const baseSchema = z.object({
  password: z.string().min(8),
  confirmPassword: z.string(),
  anotherField: z.string(),
});

const schema = baseSchema.refine(
  (data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword,
  {
    message: "Passwords do not match",
    path: ["confirmPassword"],
    when(payload) {
      return baseSchema
        .pick({ password: true, confirmPassword: true })
        .safeParse(payload.value).success;
    },
  }
);
```

const schema = z
  .object({
    password: z.string().min(8),
    confirmPassword: z.string(),
    anotherField: z.string(),
